rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t+2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t+6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-3)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}4t-1 \\\\ 3t+2 \\\\ 5t+6\\end{aligned}]+(2t-3)[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8t-2 \\\\ 6t+4 \\\\ 10t+12\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}8t-12 \\\\ 6t-9 \\\\ 10t-15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}10t-8 \\\\ 12t-4 \\\\ 6t-5\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12t-15 \\\\ 14t-7 \\\\ 18t-2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4t-7 \\\\ 3t-2 \\\\ 5t-1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}8t-14 \\\\ 6t-5 \\\\ 10t-3\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-71225" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}16t-14 \\\\ 12t-5 \\\\ 20t-3\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ {t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ t \\\\ {t}^{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{2}{{t}^{2}}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{3}{{t}^{3}}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 3t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ 4{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}+2 \\\\ {t}^{3}+3t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}t+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{3}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-70685" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ t+2t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ {t}^{2}+3{t}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}2u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=2t+2$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(2u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(3)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2(2t+2) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 4t+4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32498" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8t+8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j"] ["math" "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j"] ["math" "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,0,\\,\\frac{1}{u}⟩$ and $u(t)={e}^{2t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}0,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})=2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{u(t)},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}(t)}⟩{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}⟨\\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{1}{({e}^{2t})^{2}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{2t}},\\,0,\\,-\\frac{2{e}^{2t}}{{e}^{4t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{2t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,\\,0,\\,2{e}^{2t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,-{e}^{-4t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{-2t},\\,0,\\,{e}^{-4t}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2,\\,0,\\,-2{e}^{-2t}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=⟨\\frac{1}{u},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1),\\,1⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{t}$, then $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(g∘u)^{′}(t)=g′(u(t))u′(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\frac{1}{u}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u+1},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{(u(t))^{2}},\\,\\frac{1}{u(t)+1},\\,0⟩\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{t}{1+t},\\,0⟩\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}) \\\\  & =⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,-\\frac{t}{2+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},-\\frac{{t}^{2}}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-\\frac{t}{1+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1}{t},-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128570" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨1,-\\frac{1}{t+{t}^{2}},0⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $g(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ 5 \\\\ {u}^{2}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t$, then  $(g∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\operatorname{ln}⁡u \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,5\\,\\, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,\\,{u}^{2}\\,\\,\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)=\\frac{1}{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(g∘u)^{′}(t) & =g′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u(t)} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u(t)\\end{aligned}]{u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{t}[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32860" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-32860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{u} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2u\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32860" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t}{t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩$ and $u(t)={t}^{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(ug(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})=3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & ={t}^{3}⟨1,\\,2t,\\,6{t}^{2}⟩+3{t}^{2}⟨t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩+⟨3{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{4},\\,6{t}^{5}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-128587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{3},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t,\\,5{t}^{4},\\,3{t}^{5}⟩"] ["math" "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{2},\\,9{t}^{4}⟩"] ["math" "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩"] ["math" "⟨{t}^{4},\\,{t}^{3},\\,{t}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨4{t}^{3},\\,5{t}^{4},\\,12{t}^{5}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "60{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+14t+2"] ["math" "60{t}^{3}+7{t}^{2}+10t+2"] ["math" "80{t}^{3}+11{t}^{2}+12t+2"] ["math" "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2"] ["math" "80{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}+10t+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ and $v(t)=2t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{1}{t},\\,2t,\\,1⟩+2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,4{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩+⟨2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128586" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-128586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩"] ["math" "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,t,\\,3t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128586" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡t+1,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,2t⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(f\\times g)^{′}(t)$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨t,\\,5,\\,{t}^{4}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the cross product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\times g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t)+f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t)\\times g(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3} & t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{3} & t\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4{t}^{3} \\\\ {t}^{2} & t\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & {t}^{3}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩, \\\\ f(t)\\times {g}^{′}(t) & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ t & 5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & {t}^{4} \\\\ 3{t}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}t & {t}^{4} \\\\ 2t & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}t & 5 \\\\ 2t & 3{t}^{2}\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\times g)^{′}(t) & =⟨-4{t}^{6},\\,4{t}^{5}-t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩+⟨5-3{t}^{6},\\,2{t}^{5}-t,\\,3{t}^{3}-10t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128896" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-128896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩"] ["math" "⟨2{t}^{6}+1,\\,4{t}^{5},\\,{t}^{3}-5t⟩"] ["math" "⟨5{t}^{6},\\,{t}^{5}+4{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨7{t}^{6},\\,6{t}^{5}-5,\\,4{t}^{3}+2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨{t}^{6}-5,\\,4{t}^{5}+2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-128896" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-7{t}^{6}+5,\\,6{t}^{5}-2t,\\,4{t}^{3}-10t⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given $f(t)=({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+4{t}^{2}\\,k$, evaluate $({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(t)={f}^{″}(t)\\cdot f(t)+{f}^{′}(t)\\cdot {f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the first and second derivative of the function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-2)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2})\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+4\\cdot 2t\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+2t\\,j+8t\\,k \\\\ {f}^{″}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8t)\\,k \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2t\\,i+2j+8\\,k \\\\  & =6t\\,i+2j+8\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{′}\\cdot f)^{′}(0) & ={f}^{″}(0)\\cdot f(0)+{f}^{′}(0)\\cdot {f}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =(6(0)\\,i+2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (({0}^{3}-1)\\,i+({0}^{2}-2)\\,j+4(0)^{2}\\,k)+(3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k)\\cdot (3(0)^{2}\\,i+2(0)\\,j+8(0)\\,k) \\\\  & =(2\\,j+8\\,k)\\cdot (-i-2\\,j) \\\\  & =0(-1)+2(-2)+(0) \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32837" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83"} {"question" "q-32837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4"] ["math" "-8"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "q-32837" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "db777a0a467482460986067e67bee8c2f502ccfff1c1ba3dfce74096e4652a9d"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "01b8d6499d07800eb9b95f8bce49f334319a3950ef97980325140762f936b5f8"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "01b8d6499d07800eb9b95f8bce49f334319a3950ef97980325140762f936b5f8"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where $[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t) = t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "48bd0d854cfb4f4319ba0bcfc20e901ab2343a3894412ce6ed3bd30967428aa3"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "48bd0d854cfb4f4319ba0bcfc20e901ab2343a3894412ce6ed3bd30967428aa3"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "765bde555a8bc807f976fac78ce3f31bcead1429fa6f4d87a1da8767a5281b76"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "765bde555a8bc807f976fac78ce3f31bcead1429fa6f4d87a1da8767a5281b76"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "485f507a0ab0ee75c27ca3bacaf1d175187229531f900b14fab6eef945434caf"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "485f507a0ab0ee75c27ca3bacaf1d175187229531f900b14fab6eef945434caf"}] "usage" {"q-32298" [] "e-2477" [] "q-32498" [] "e-2480" [] "e-2479" [] "e-2478" []} "basis" 1409 "retractions" [[17592186115680 :question/problem "If \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f} ( u ) = \\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 3\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n and $u(t) = 2t + 2$, then $( \\mathbf{f} \\circ  u {)}^{\\prime } ( t ) =$"] [17592186115680 :question/worked-solution "The chain rule gives $(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'=\\mathbf f'(u(t))u'(t)$. Since $\\mathbf f'(u)=\\langle2,2u,0\\rangle$ and $u'(t)=2$, $$(\\mathbf f\\circ u)'(t)=2\\langle2,2(2t+2),0\\rangle=\\langle4,8t+8,0\\rangle.$$"] [17592186115677 :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g)'(t)$, where $$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f(t)&=20t\\mathbf i-2t\\mathbf j+(2+5t)\\mathbf k,\\\\\\mathbf g(t)&=t^3\\mathbf i+t\\mathbf j+(t^2+t)\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}$$"] [17592186115677 :question/worked-solution "First form the dot product: $$\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g=20t^4-2t^2+(2+5t)(t^2+t)=20t^4+5t^3+5t^2+2t.$$ Differentiating gives $$(\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g)'=80t^3+15t^2+10t+2.$$"] [17592186114884 :question/problem "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t)+2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t$, where $$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f(t)&=(4t^2+9)\\mathbf i-\\frac1{t-2}\\mathbf j+\\cos(2t)\\mathbf k,\\\\\\mathbf g(t)&=(4t-1)\\mathbf i+e^{3t}\\mathbf j+\\cos(2t)\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}$$"] [17592186114884 :question/worked-solution "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\mathbf{f}}^{\\prime } ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( 4 {t}^{2} + 9 ) \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( - \\frac{1}{t - 2} ) \\, \\mathbf{j} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\cos   2 t ) \\, \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = 8 t \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{( t - 2 {)}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} , \\\\ {\\mathbf{g}}^{\\prime } ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( 4 t - 1 ) \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( {e}^{3 t} ) \\mathbf{j} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\cos   2 t ) \\mathbf{k} \\\\  & = 4 \\, \\mathbf{i} + 3 {e}^{3 t} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}( \\mathbf{f} ( t ) + 2 \\mathbf{g} ( t ) {)}^{\\prime } & = {\\mathbf{f}}^{\\prime } ( t ) + 2 {\\mathbf{g}}^{\\prime } ( t ) \\\\  & = ( 8 t \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{( t - 2 {)}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} ) + 2 ( 4 \\, \\mathbf{i} + 3 {e}^{3 t} \\, \\mathbf{j} - 2 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} ) \\\\  & = 8 ( t + 1 ) \\, \\mathbf{i} + ( \\frac{1}{( t - 2 {)}^{2}} + 6 {e}^{3 t} ) \\, \\mathbf{j} - 6 \\sin   2 t \\, \\mathbf{k} .\\end{array}$$"] [17592186114885 :question/problem "Find $(u(t)\\mathbf g(t))'$, where $\\mathbf g(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}\\ln t\\\\-t\\\\e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $u(t)=t$."] [17592186114885 :question/worked-solution "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big(u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t)$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ng^{\\prime }(t) &= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{d}{dt}(\\ln t) \\\\ \\frac{d}{dt}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{d}{dt}e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\nu^{\\prime }(t) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(t) = 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(u(t)g(t))^{\\prime } &= u^{\\prime }(t)g(t) + u(t)g^{\\prime }(t) \\\\\n&= 1 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\ln t \\\\ -t \\\\ e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} + t \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\ln t \\\\ -t \\\\ e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2te^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 + \\ln t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t + 1)e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186114886 :question/problem "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t)$, if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3$."] [17592186114886 :question/worked-solution "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t)\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{\\prime }(u) &= \\frac{d}{du}(\\ln u)i + \\frac{d}{du}(u^{2} + 5)j + \\frac{d}{du}(4u)k \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{u}i + 2uj + 4k, \\\\\nu^{\\prime }(t) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(2t^{3}) = 6t^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}( \\mathbf{f} \\circ  u {)}^{\\prime } ( t ) & = {\\mathbf{f}}^{\\prime } ( u ( t ) ) {u}^{\\prime } ( t ) \\\\  & = ( \\frac{1}{u ( t )} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 2 u ( t ) \\, \\mathbf{j} + 4 \\, \\mathbf{k} ) {u}^{\\prime } ( t ) \\\\  & = ( \\frac{1}{2 {t}^{3}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 2 ( 2 {t}^{3} ) \\, \\mathbf{j} + 4 \\, \\mathbf{k} ) \\cdot  6 {t}^{2} \\\\  & = \\frac{3}{t} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 24 {t}^{5} \\, \\mathbf{j} + 24 {t}^{2} \\, \\mathbf{k} .\\end{array}$$"] [17592186114887 :question/problem "Find $\\dfrac{d}{dt}(\\mathbf f\\cdot\\mathbf g)(t)$, where $$\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf f(t)&=\\sqrt t\\,\\mathbf i+t^2\\mathbf j,\\\\\\mathbf g(t)&=\\frac1t\\mathbf i+e^t\\mathbf j.\\end{aligned}$$"] [17592186114887 :question/worked-solution "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} \\mathbf{f} ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\sqrt{t} ) \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( {t}^{2} ) \\mathbf{j} \\\\  & = \\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{t}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + 2 t \\, \\mathbf{j} , \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} \\mathbf{g} ( t ) & = \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( \\frac{1}{t} ) \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d} t} ( {e}^{t} ) \\mathbf{j} \\\\  & = - \\frac{1}{{t}^{2}} \\, \\mathbf{i} + {e}^{t} \\, \\mathbf{j} .\\end{array}$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t) &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\\\[3pt] &= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) + \\left(\\sqrt{t} \\, \\mathbf i + t^2 \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2} \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\\\[3pt] &=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}} +2te^t + \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right) + t^2e^t \\\\[3pt] &=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} - \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t + t^2e^t \\\\[3pt] &= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t. \\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186113463 17592186113464 17592186113465 17592186113466 17592186113467 17592186113481 17592186113482 17592186113483 17592186113484 17592186113485] "immutable_fields" [[17592186113462 :answer-field/correct] [17592186113462 :answer-field/id] [17592186113462 :answer-field/key] [17592186113462 :answer-field/type] [17592186113480 :answer-field/correct] [17592186113480 :answer-field/id] [17592186113480 :answer-field/key] [17592186113480 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
